# Top-k frequent: count with a map, push (-count, x) tuples into a min-heap, pop k.
# Ties pop in ascending order of x, since tuples compare element by element.
x = [1,1,1,2,2,3,4,4,4,4,5,5]
c = [->] ?? 0; x{c@_+=1}
q = PQ[]; c{q+=(-_,@)}
println:0..3{q.pop@1}
t = split:"the quick fox and the lazy dog and the fox"," "
n = [->] ?? 0; t{n@_+=1}
p = PQ[]; n{p+=(-_,@)}
println:0..3{p.pop@1}.join:" "
